==Trivia==
* This location is based on the Russian "Арктика" (Arktika) nuclear-powered icebreaker.
* Initially, the icebreaker was called "Северный ветер" (North Wind) in concept art. In subsequent screenshots, the landing pad read "Сибирь" (Siberia). In the final trailer, the name was changed to "Борей" (Boreas). In ancient Greek mythology, Boreas is the personification of the stormy northern wind. Boreas was also considered the god of winter, descending from the cold mountains of Thrace, cooling the air with his icy breath.
<li style="display: inline-block;"><gallery widths="300" heights="169" mode="packed">
File:Icebreaker North Wind Name.png|"Северный ветер" (North Wind) early concept art
File:Icebreaker Siberia Name.jpg|"Сибирь" (Siberia) late concept art
File:Icebreaker Boreas Name.png|"Борей" (Boreas) in the teaser trailer
</gallery></li>
* During the "[[Events#Full_Speed_Ahead_(15_May_2026)|Full Speed Ahead]]" event, it becomes clear that the [[Rogues]] know about the icebreaker and where to find it, specifically somewhere off the coast of the Gulf of Finland, near [[Tarkov]]. This is revealed by [[Rogue intel maps]], which can be found on [[Knight]].

